title: 'pallet-validator-collators: random draw of validator collators under a cap'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    When `MaxCollators` is set, `pallet-validator-collators` draws the validators at random at the
    first of the two forced rotations after a set arrives. The draw shuffles the whole set with a
    seed made of the genesis hash, the era and the relay chain epoch randomness, keeps the
    validators with registered keys and truncates to the cap. The drawn list and its era are
    stored in the new `Collators` storage item and reported in the new `CollatorsDrawn` event.
    Without a cap every validator with registered keys is returned.

    Changing the cap while a set is stored forces two session rotations. The first draws the list
    anew from the stored set, with the randomness cached at that time. Removing the cap clears the
    drawn list.

    The pallet implements `cumulus_pallet_parachain_system::OnSystemEvent` and caches the relay
    chain `ONE_EPOCH_AGO_RANDOMNESS` in the new `EpochRandomness` storage item. Runtimes using the
    pallet must include it in the `OnSystemEvent` of `cumulus-pallet-parachain-system`, alone or
    in a tuple with other handlers, and should return the keys of `Pallet::relay_keys_to_prove`
    from `cumulus_primitives_core::KeyToIncludeInRelayProof`. A relay chain state proof that lacks
    the trie nodes of the randomness key, or holds a value that does not decode, makes the block
    invalid. A proof that shows the key absent, as before the relay chain's first epoch change,
    caches the zero value a draw without randomness uses.

    Asset Hub Westend and People Westend wire the pallet as `OnSystemEvent` and implement
    `KeyToIncludeInRelayProof` with its keys.
crates:
- name: pallet-validator-collators
  bump: major
- name: asset-hub-westend-runtime
  bump: minor
- name: people-westend-runtime
  bump: minor
- name: people-westend-integration-tests
  bump: none
